  "articleBody": "Start by documenting the existing kitchen, defining which connections will remain, and deciding whether the replacement includes countertops, flooring, lighting, or layout changes. A clear scope helps a design-build team prepare a more useful plan and reduces surprises caused by hidden conditions, specialty storage, uneven walls, or work that falls outside a simple cabinet swap.",
